 :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-949efed5-cf98-5f5d-b7b8-a1053d135c13" :answer-field/id #uuid "949efed5-cf98-5f5d-b7b8-a1053d135c13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cbac1d5e-aa32-595d-aef2-4b642a419a04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cbac1d5e-aa32-595d-aef2-4b642a419a04"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbac1d5e-aa32-595d-aef2-4b642a419a04" :answer/id #uuid "cbac1d5e-aa32-595d-aef2-4b642a419a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143175 :question/problem "Expressed as a whole number, $4÷\\frac{4}{5}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $4$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{4}{5}$ is $\\frac{5}{4}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n4÷\\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{4}{1}÷\\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{4\\times 5}{1\\times 4}=\\frac{20}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n20÷4=5\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186140337 :answer-field/correct "answer-e41865a1-693f-534b-8947-4f269f3ab305" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e41865a1-693f-534b-8947-4f269f3ab305"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e41865a1-693f-534b-8947-4f269f3ab305" :answer/id #uuid "e41865a1-693f-534b-8947-4f269f3ab305" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-956a3f23-3712-563b-a380-795700cc20ae" :question/id #uuid "956a3f23-3712-563b-a380-795700cc20ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-211448" :question/problem "Expressed as a whole number, $6÷\\frac{3}{4}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $6$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n6=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{4}$ is $\\frac{4}{3}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{6}{1}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{6\\times 4}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{24}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n24÷3=8\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f44398f3-65e2-5030-a777-61de82751708"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f44398f3-65e2-5030-a777-61de82751708" :answer-field/id #uuid "f44398f3-65e2-5030-a777-61de82751708" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e1d78198-a05d-5ebe-bc81-d0050bb9b711" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1d78198-a05d-5ebe-bc81-d0050bb9b711"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1d78198-a05d-5ebe-bc81-d0050bb9b711" :answer/id #uuid "e1d78198-a05d-5ebe-bc81-d0050bb9b711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-74bacbf6-b03a-5e84-a6aa-342811a3c626" :question/id #uuid "74bacbf6-b03a-5e84-a6aa-342811a3c626" :question/math-academy-id "q-211475" :question/problem "Expressed as an mixed number in its lowest terms, $3÷\\frac{6}{7}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{6}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{6}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{3}{1}÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6} & =\\frac{3}{6}\\times \\frac{7}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert our result to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{2}=3\\,\\text{R}\\,1=3\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24de7c5f-c1dc-5245-9a97-7581534ce82f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24de7c5f-c1dc-5245-9a97-7581534ce82f" :answer-field/id #uuid "24de7c5f-c1dc-5245-9a97-7581534ce82f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f1b7f2ee-4209-53d9-95c4-028e69600537" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1b7f2ee-4209-53d9-95c4-028e69600537"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1b7f2ee-4209-53d9-95c4-028e69600537" :answer/id #uuid "f1b7f2ee-4209-53d9-95c4-028e69600537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143240 :question/problem "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, $2÷\\frac{6}{7}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{6}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{6}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{2}{1}÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6} & =\\frac{2}{6}\\times \\frac{7}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\times 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert our result to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}=2\\,\\text{R}\\,1=2\\,\\frac{1}{3}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186140486 :answer-field/correct "answer-33e34223-307e-5cf9-a09a-64998b582c67" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33e34223-307e-5cf9-a09a-64998b582c67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33e34223-307e-5cf9-a09a-64998b582c67" :answer/id #uuid "33e34223-307e-5cf9-a09a-64998b582c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9cccdde7-11a3-5e93-bfcd-4d97bbb04b46" :question/id #uuid "9cccdde7-11a3-5e93-bfcd-4d97bbb04b46" :question/math-academy-id "q-57350" :question/problem "$3÷\\frac{6}{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{6}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{6}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{3}{1}÷\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{6} & =\\frac{3}{6}\\times \\frac{7}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 7 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fcae4ef9-b956-5a61-8936-0e4dd16f2526"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fcae4ef9-b956-5a61-8936-0e4dd16f2526" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcae4ef9-b956-5a61-8936-0e4dd16f2526" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ec2eab6e-ec9a-5f16-833e-07b634fa0cba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39bb3e28-def5-5b95-a7af-a74115ab33c7" "answer-100ceea8-3703-5dff-a1bd-331a1045f8dd" "answer-ec2eab6e-ec9a-5f16-833e-07b634fa0cba" "answer-6a1999f7-a8f0-5ab9-9e8f-ce0c4c751313" "answer-9c32f8ea-5595-5a77-aca5-ef2a8d3f316a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39bb3e28-def5-5b95-a7af-a74115ab33c7" :answer/id #uuid "39bb3e28-def5-5b95-a7af-a74115ab33c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-100ceea8-3703-5dff-a1bd-331a1045f8dd" :answer/id #uuid "100ceea8-3703-5dff-a1bd-331a1045f8dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec2eab6e-ec9a-5f16-833e-07b634fa0cba" :answer/id #uuid "ec2eab6e-ec9a-5f16-833e-07b634fa0cba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a1999f7-a8f0-5ab9-9e8f-ce0c4c751313" :answer/id #uuid "6a1999f7-a8f0-5ab9-9e8f-ce0c4c751313" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c32f8ea-5595-5a77-aca5-ef2a8d3f316a" :answer/id #uuid "9c32f8ea-5595-5a77-aca5-ef2a8d3f316a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143239 :question/problem "Expressed as an improper fraction in its lowest terms, $6÷\\frac{8}{11}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $6$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n6=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{8}{11}$ is $\\frac{11}{8}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{8}{11}=\\frac{6}{1}÷\\frac{8}{11}=\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{11}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{11}{8} & =\\frac{6}{8}\\times \\frac{11}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\times 11 \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186140485 :answer-field/correct "answer-71d7cab0-fe11-5561-bc9e-de01894e92fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71d7cab0-fe11-5561-bc9e-de01894e92fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71d7cab0-fe11-5561-bc9e-de01894e92fe" :answer/id #uuid "71d7cab0-fe11-5561-bc9e-de01894e92fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{33}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f41233c3-116b-5b5c-aed9-7d13e659c7e0" :question/id #uuid "f41233c3-116b-5b5c-aed9-7d13e659c7e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-211468" :question/problem "Expressed as an improper fraction in its lowest terms, $2÷\\frac{8}{9}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $2$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2=\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{8}{9}$ is $\\frac{9}{8}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{8}{9}=\\frac{2}{1}÷\\frac{8}{9}=\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{9}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{1}\\times \\frac{9}{8} & =\\frac{2}{8}\\times \\frac{9}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\times 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7c5ee2cf-2973-5656-bf9f-53588d2c806c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7c5ee2cf-2973-5656-bf9f-53588d2c806c" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c5ee2cf-2973-5656-bf9f-53588d2c806c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-927932fb-f7cb-572a-91af-71f6e7ecd4c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-927932fb-f7cb-572a-91af-71f6e7ecd4c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-927932fb-f7cb-572a-91af-71f6e7ecd4c5" :answer/id #uuid "927932fb-f7cb-572a-91af-71f6e7ecd4c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144069 :tutorial/content "To divide a whole number by a *unit* fraction, we multiply the whole number by the fraction's denominator. \n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{2}}\\div \\dfrac 1{\\color{blue}{3}} = {\\color{red}{2}}\\times {\\color{blue}{3}} = 6.\n$$\n\nNow, note the following:\n\n- ${\\color{blue}{3}}$ is the *reciprocal* of $\\dfrac1{\\color{blue}{3}}.$\n\n- So, to calculate ${\\color{red}{2}}\\div \\dfrac 1{\\color{blue}{3}},$ we multiplied $\\color{red}2$ by the *reciprocal* of $\\dfrac1{\\color{blue}{3}}.$\n\nThinking about division in terms of reciprocals will help us later when we want to divide whole numbers by non-unit fractions." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144070 :tutorial/content "When dividing a whole number by a non-unit fraction, we can still use the same technique of multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction. \n\nThe only difference is that, in order to perform the multiplication, we must convert the whole number into an improper fraction.\n\nTo illustrate, let's compute $3\\div \\dfrac 2 9 .$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3=\\dfrac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\color{blue}2}{\\color{red}9}$ is $\\dfrac{\\color{red}9}{\\color{blue}2}  .$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n3\\div \\dfrac 2 9 = \n\n\\dfrac 3 1 \\div \\dfrac{\\color{blue}2}{\\color{red}9} = \\dfrac 3 1 \\times  \\dfrac{\\color{red}9}{\\color{blue}2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\dfrac 3 {1} \\times \\dfrac{9}{2} =  \\dfrac {3\\times 9} {1\\times 2} = \\dfrac{27}{2}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144097 :tutorial/content "Let's find the value of $8\\div \\dfrac 4 5.$\n\nDividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $8$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n8=\\dfrac{8}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}5}$ is $\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{blue}4}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n8\\div \\dfrac 4 5 = \n\\dfrac 8 1 \\div \\dfrac{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}5} = \\dfrac 8 1 \\times  \\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{blue}4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\dfrac 8 {1} \\times \\dfrac{5}{4} =  \\dfrac {8\\times 5} {1\\times 4} = \\dfrac{40}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n40 \\div 4 = 10.\n$$\n\nSometimes, we may wish to use a fraction multiplication strategy to simplify the problem *before* multiplying the fractions. Let's see an example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143012 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
